nuwa r12: mount the SystemOS cryptex read-only on /private/preboot and hand the
initproc an environment that points dyld at the shared cache inside it.

Why: the 20H392 OS window has neither /System/Library/Caches/com.apple.dyld nor
/usr/lib/libSystem.B.dylib (host apfs-fuse read of out/root-inputs-20261113/
os-window.raw); both live in the Cryptex1,SystemOS window, which the UFS driver
already publishes but nothing mounts.  Without the mount, dyld fails at
"no shared cache file" and iOS cannot resolve libSystem at all.

Shape (deliberately the official non-union form of
patches/xnu/offline-owner-systemos-mount.patch, without the owner boot manifest):

  * mount("apfs", "/private/preboot", MNT_RDONLY, <0x150-byte user-mount payload>)
  * envp for the first exec: DYLD_SHARED_CACHE_DIR=/private/preboot/System/Library/
    Caches/com.apple.dyld
  * every failure records a stage/errno and continues; the kernel never panics here
    (the boot progress page shows the result instead).

Apply order: after 8796-nuwa-exec-policy-skip.patch and
8796-nuwa-boot-progress.patch (their anchors are in this file).  Opt-in:
-DXNU_NUWA_SYSTEMOS_MOUNT=1.  The implementation lives in the device tree at
package/nuwa-systemos/nuwa_systemos.c (bsd object), not in this patch.
